From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375-motorola-rhodep: add ramoops

Add a pstore/ramoops region so that the tail of the kernel log and any
panic survive a reboot. Without this a bootloop is undebuggable: the ABL
rewrites the cmdline to console=null, so nothing reaches a serial console
either, and there is no way to see why the kernel died.

After a failed boot, flash a kernel that does boot (which also needs this
node) and read /sys/fs/pstore/.

The address is the one the vendor device tree uses (holi.dtsi: ramoops at
0xd0000000, 2 MiB), so it is known not to be clobbered by the bootloader.
It sits inside the DDR range declared in the memory node
(0x80000000 + 0x80000000) and does not overlap any other reserved region.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -99,6 +99,25 @@
 			reg = <0 0x85200000 0 0xc00000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * Black box for debugging boot loops: pstore/ramoops keeps the tail
+		 * of the console log and the panic in RAM, and both survive a
+		 * reboot. After a failed boot they can be read from a kernel that
+		 * does boot, under /sys/fs/pstore/.
+		 *
+		 * This is the address the vendor DT uses (holi.dtsi: ramoops at
+		 * 0xd0000000, 2 MiB), so the bootloader is known not to scribble
+		 * over it.
+		 */
+		ramoops@d0000000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0xd0000000 0x0 0x200000>;
+			record-size = <0x8000>;
+			console-size = <0x100000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x8000>;
+			ecc-size = <16>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	panel_vci: panel-vci-regulator {
